You must be thinking of some other game which also has something
called "explore mode".  In NetHack, explore mode is just like the
normal game, except:

* your score doesn't go into the high score file
* with a very small number of exceptions, you can choose not to die
  when something would kill you.  (You get a prompt: Die? (y/n))
* if you start the game in explore mode, you start with a wand of
  wishing.

That's it; the game is otherwise identical.  (Of course, that's a lot
of making the game easier, which lets you "explore" what's out there
without having to worry so much about permanent consequences.)


